Z||000005||Raydar||10-26-2001||09:47 AM||||This is a pic that Aus posted a couple of days ago of the Holden Monaro. This is widely reported to be the platform to be used for the Camaro replacement. <BR> <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Dcp_0247.jpg">   <P>According to Aus, they are going to drop the Monaro name and call it a GTO (for Australian consumption). One can only guess what it will be called here, or how it will be changed for US consumption. <P>Having said all that, let me get to the real point...<BR>I wonder why Motor Trend happened to post that pic of the Banshee. <BR>Think it might be a teaser, now that Pontiac is talking with GM about producing a car at the Bowling Green facility? <BR>Could it happen?<BR>(I really did read that. Don't remember where, though. And I'm gonna keep repeating it until someone proves I'm in error.)<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT><p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 10-26-2001).]||||reg||14
