Z||000014||AusFiero||10-26-2001||06:53 PM||||Yes I have seen the car. I took the shot of the yellow one. The Commodore coupe / Monaro is a large car by Australian standards but the wheel base doesn't look any bigger than a 4th generation Firebird. Holden will be calling it the Monaro for their versions but HSV (Holden Special Vehicles who are seperate to Holden) intend to call their versions the GTS and the GTO. It would actually make a better GTO replacement stateside rather than an F Body. The size of it and style in my reckoning is more GTO like. Large car, full size boot and higher slung than a Firebird.<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/ausfiero2.gif">    <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A> | <A HREF="http://www.fieroshop.com.au" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Accessories</A>||202.139.20.3||reg||1
Z||000015||Rick 88||10-27-2001||12:15 AM||||Back in 64 Vette's had 327's. As I recall the Banshee's had Pontiac 326's or the 4-bbl Sprint version of their Overhead Cam straight six. A 389 would have bolted in but GTO production used up all the availability. A Tri-Power 389 Banshee would have given the Vette fits!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>I like the ideal of the LS1 6-speed Holden GTO. The base version uses a SC 3800 engine with rear drive independent suspension! I would buy a GTO over a version of the F bodies if it was available in the U.S. If you check out the Holden site it has nice pics of the interior as well. Maybe we should get some of GM's Australian stylists to help out over here.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Rick 88<p>[This message has been edited by Rick 88 (edited 10-27-2001).]||||reg||12
